resources/js/components/zone-manager.js:
  - Add state next to zipCodes (:262-266): `selectedZip: null`, `zipListeners: {}`, `detachNotice: ''`.
  - NEW `attachZipHandlers(zip, overlays)` — factors out the duplicated listener wiring that
    today exists at TWO sites, :434 (hydrateZips) and :640 (addZip). Both currently read
    `overlays.forEach(o => o.addListener('click', () => this.removeZip(zip)))`; both are
    replaced by `this.attachZipHandlers(zip, overlays)`. The helper attaches ONLY
    `o.addListener('click', () => this.selectZip(zip))`. This is the whole of AC7: the plain
    map click no longer reaches removeZip.
  - NEW `selectZip(zip)`:
      if (this.drawing) return;
      if (this.selectedZip && this.selectedZip !== zip) this.deselectZip();
      const overlays = this.zipOverlays[zip]; if (!overlays) return;
      this.selectedZip = zip;
      this.zipListeners[zip] = [];
      overlays.forEach(o => {
          o.setOptions({ ...this.editablePolygonStyle('#059669') });   // editable:true -> Google
                                                                        // renders vertex +
                                                                        // midpoint handles (AC4)
          const path = o.getPath();
          ['set_at', 'insert_at', 'remove_at'].forEach(evt => {
              this.zipListeners[zip].push(
                  google.maps.event.addListener(path, evt, () => this.detachZip(zip))
              );
          });
      });
    Green (#059669) is kept on selection so the user can still tell it came from a ZIP.
  - NEW `deselectZip()` — restores `this.zipStyle()` on the currently selected overlays,
    removes the stored path listeners via google.maps.event.removeListener, clears
    this.zipListeners[zip] and this.selectedZip.
  - NEW `detachZip(zip)`:
      const overlays = this.zipOverlays[zip];
      if (!overlays) return;                    // idempotent: set_at fires repeatedly per drag
      (this.zipListeners[zip] || []).forEach(l => google.maps.event.removeListener(l));
      delete this.zipListeners[zip];
      delete this.zipOverlays[zip];
      this.zipCodes = this.zipCodes.filter(z => z !== zip);
      if (this.selectedZip === zip) this.selectedZip = null;
      overlays.forEach(o => {
          o.setOptions(this.editablePolygonStyle('#2563eb'));   // now a drawn polygon
          this.attachEditablePolygonHandlers(o);                 // subsequent edits sync normally
          this.polygonOverlays.push(o);
      });
      this.detachNotice = `ZIP ${zip} is now a custom boundary — its ZIP chip was removed.`;
      this.syncEditingState();
    Note ALL rings of a multi-ring ZIP are promoted together (renderEditableZip :446-459
    creates one overlay per ring), otherwise editing one ring would silently drop the others.
  - `removeZip(zip)` (:658) — before deleting, call the same listener cleanup and clear
    selectedZip if it matches, so the chip '×' path leaks nothing. Its behaviour is otherwise
    unchanged; it stays wired to the chip '×' (blade :157) and handleZipBackspace (:653) only.
  - `clearEditing()` (:580) and `tearDownEditing()` (:478) — reset selectedZip, drop all
    zipListeners, and clear detachNotice alongside the existing zipCodes/zipOverlays reset.
  - `beginEdit()` (:340) — clear detachNotice at the top so a notice cannot survive a zone switch.

