DRIVER AMENDMENT (session B) — `deselectZip()` MUST pass `editable: false` explicitly.
`zipStyle()` (zone-manager.js:550-558) returns NO `editable` key at all, and
google.maps.Polygon.setOptions() applies only the keys present in the object it is given. So
`o.setOptions(this.zipStyle())` leaves `editable: true` in place: the overlay looks deselected
but still shows vertex handles, and a stray drag still fires set_at and detaches a ZIP the user
believed they had deselected. Write it as:
    o.setOptions({ ...this.zipStyle(), editable: false });
Verified by the driver against source. The drawn-polygon path does not have this asymmetry --
`editablePolygonStyle(color)` (:538-548) DOES carry `editable: true` explicitly, so the
`this.editablePolygonStyle('#059669')` call in `selectZip()` is valid as written.
